      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are reviewing one task's implementation for spec compliance and code quality. Task-scoped gate.\n\n## What Was Requested\nRead the task brief: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-9-brief.md`\n\nConstraints (storage.md §6 two-phase migration policy):\n- `dbm/alembic/env.py` sets `target_metadata = Base.metadata` and supports offline+online modes.\n- `operations.py`: `alembic_config(cfg)` builds an alembic `Config` with `script_location` = the dbm/alembic dir and `sqlalchemy.url` = cfg.dsn. `init(cfg, force=False)`: force → drop_all+create_all (returns \"recreated\"); else if our tables already exist → \"exists\" (no-op); else if migration versions exist → `command.upgrade(head)`, else `create_all` → \"created\". `migrate(cfg, sql=False)` → upgrade head. `revision(cfg, message, autogenerate=True)`. `status(cfg)` returns dict with keys including `revision`, `head`, `drift` (via MigrationContext + compare_metadata). `seed`/`import_dump` are the deferred stubs (import_dump raises NotImplementedError).\n- Services never migrate at startup; only these CLI-invoked verbs do.\n- No \"Claude\" anywhere. TDD.\n\n## Implementer Report\n`/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-9-report.md` — unverified claims. IGNORE its mention of a \"golden-DDL failure\": the controller root-caused that as a separate flaky test (nondeterministic index order in a DIFFERENT file, cli_schema_dump.py) and already fixed it; it is NOT part of this task and the full suite is now green (74 passed, 7 skipped).\n\n## Diff Under Review\nBase: bdcae06  Head: 81aeb43\nDiff file: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/review-bdcae06..81aeb43.diff`\nRead the diff file once. Do not re-run git or crawl the codebase. Read-only.\n\n## Tests\n`test_operations.py` is `@requires_db` and all 3 tests SKIP without `TALIUM_TEST_DSN` (expected). So the DB behavior of init/migrate/status is NOT exercised by CI here — judge correctness by reading the code. The controller confirmed `from server.storage.dbm import operations` imports cleanly.\n\n## Focus points (judge by reading, since tests skip)\n- `init` phase-1/phase-2 branching correctness; does the \"exists\" no-op check use the right table set (`Base.metadata.tables` vs actual DB tables)?\n- `alembic_config` correctness (script_location resolvable to the dbm/alembic dir; url set).\n- `status` using MigrationContext + compare_metadata + ScriptDirectory head — correct API usage?\n- `env.py` offline/online modes, target_metadata wiring.\n- `import_dump` clearly deferred (raises with a clear message).\n\n## Output Format\n### Spec Compliance — ✅ | ❌ (file:line) | ⚠️ Cannot verify (e.g. DB-only behavior — say what a DB run should check)\n### Strengths\n### Issues — Critical / Important / Minor (file:line, what, why, fix)\n### Assessment — **Task quality:** Approved | Needs fixes; **Reasoning:** 1-2 sentences.\nBegin directly with the verdict.",
